# CONTROL's reader. The same two lines as the attack, pointed at a source nothing
# labeled.
#
# /scratch, not /untrusted. The bytes are a report, the report asks for a config
# change, the reader forwards it to ops, and ops applies it -- the identical chain,
# the identical privileged call, allowed. Nothing in the actions distinguishes this
# from peer-reader-injected.actions except where the reader read from.
#
# That is the claim rung 3 has to survive, and it is why CONTROL does not simply
# send an empty message: a demo where the legitimate case asks for nothing proves
# only that doing nothing is permitted.

read-source /scratch/benign-report.txt --obey-instructions

send-agent --from-source /scratch/benign-report.txt ops
